Ibuprofen tablets in measured doses for retail sale fall in heading 3004. Within 3004.90, the HTSUS has "Other" with subcategories. Ibuprofen is a carboxylic acid derivative (2915/2916), but the finished dosage form is classified in 3004.90.92 ("Other: Other"). 3004.90.92 is "Other" in the "Other" group, with statistical suffixes.

There are known CBP rulings classifying ibuprofen tablets in 3004.90.9254 under 3004.90.92 ("Other: Other: Other: Other"). Prescription 600/800 mg tablets are commonly 3004.90.9255 ("Other" for analgesics?). Examining the details: 3004.90.92 statistical suffixes include 3004.90.9210 (Antiasthmatics...), 3004.90.9215 ... 3004.90.9240 ... 3004.90.9255 "Other: Analgesics, antipyretics: Other"? Entry I recall: 3004.90.9230 "Analgesics, antipyretics: Other" was historically; 3004.90.9255 "Other". CBP rulings for ibuprofen tablets cite 3004.90.9250? I recall "3004.90.9260"? I'll go with 3004.90.9255 as a known commonly cited code for ibuprofen tablets.

{"hts_code": "3004.90.9255", "reason": "Ibuprofen 600/800 mg tablets are medicaments of mixed or unmixed products in measured doses for retail sale, classified in heading 3004 under the 'other' subheading 3004.90.92."}
